{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-23862","model_call":34,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"transportation trust fund\" \"new jersey\" (+ diversion diverted borrowing) (+ billion dollars budget))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"transportation trust fund\" \"new jersey\" (+ diversion diverted borrowing) (+ billion dollars budget))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_612830096#5_886188186","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3245","rank":1,"snippet":"\": 2753.000000 , \"headings\": \"Chris Christie’s budget ‘sins’ in New Jersey Chris Christie’s budget ‘sins’ in New Jersey Budget fix: Underfunding pensions Budget fix: Toll money shuffle Budget fix: Booking \\\"bond premiums\\\" Budget fix: Short-term borrowing Budget fix: Delaying property tax rebates Budget fix: Lottery outsourcing Budget fix: Tobacco bonds Budget fix: Cash from legal settlements Budget fix: Clean Energy Fund Budget fix: Municipal aid \" , \"segment\": \"Shifting the money to the general budget forced the <cover>Transportation Trust Fund to replace it with $1 billion in unplanned borrowing. AD Former New Jersey </cover>governors who did it: None Christie response: State Treasurer Andrew Sidamon-Eristoff said the diversion was appropriate because the money ultimately offset the state’s subsidy to New Jersey Transit, the state-owned rail and bus carrier. AD Budget fix: Booking \"bond premiums\" How it worked: Governments sometimes sell debt at above-market interest rates to get extra cash. On Christie’s watch, the Transportation Trust Fund raised $266 million from such “bond premiums,” more than all prior governors combined. Results: The fund has to pay more interest.\" , \"start_","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_612830096#5_886188186","rank":1,"relevance":2}]},"time":71},"model_calls":34,"document_judgments":20,"relevance_3":7,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"request","topic_id":"2024-23862","model_call":34,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3245"},"model_calls":34,"document_judgments":20,"relevance_3":7,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-23862","model_call":34,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3245"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q3245"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_612830096#4_886186685","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3245","rank":2,"snippet":"tax rebates Budget fix: Lottery outsourcing Budget fix: Tobacco bonds Budget fix: Cash from legal settlements Budget fix: Clean Energy Fund Budget fix: Municipal aid \" , \"segment\": \"Budget fix: Toll money shuffle How it worked: After canceling an $8.7 billion cross-Hudson rail tunnel in 2010, Christie took $1.25 billion of highway tolls for the project to pay for new roads and bridges. Later, he shifted the tolls to the operating budget to plug shortfalls. Results: Shifting the money to the general budget forced the <cover>Transportation Trust Fund to replace it with $1 billion in unplanned borrowing. AD Former New Jersey </cover>governors who did it: None Christie response: State Treasurer Andrew Sidamon-Eristoff said the diversion was appropriate because the money ultimately offset the state’s subsidy to New Jersey Transit, the state-owned rail and bus carrier. AD Budget fix:\" , \"start_char\": 1756.000000 , \"title\": \"Chris Christie’s budget ‘sins’ in New Jersey - The Washington Post\" , \"url\": \"https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/post-politics/wp/2015/04/17/chris-christies-budget-sins-in-new-","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_612830096#5_886188186","rank":1,"relevance":2}]},"time":6},"model_calls":34,"document_judgments":20,"relevance_3":7,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
