{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-23862","model_call":61,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"state auditor\" (+ transportation highway transit rail) (+ \"cost overruns\" mismanagement waste wasted) (+ million billion dollars funds))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"state auditor\" (+ transportation highway transit rail) (+ \"cost overruns\" mismanagement waste wasted) (+ million billion dollars funds))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1715637950#5_1834801894","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3268","rank":1,"snippet":"\"The process was restarted in September 2017 and is expected to take eighteen months. The first major contract, estimated at $400 million, was awarded in May 2018. The final cost has grown from preliminary projections of $4 billion in 2006 to between $9 billion and $10 <cover>billion by 2017. Critics have called for a \"forensic audit\" to establish the cause of the increase. The tax increase legislation passed in 2017 also requires the State auditor carry out an audit of the project's accounts and to consider alternatives for completing the system. Contents 1 History 1.1 Previous projects 1.2 Studies 1.3 Impact on Honolulu mayoral elections 1.4 Delays and cost overruns 1.5 Testing and more delays 1.6 Burial issues 1.7 Social impact 2 Financing 2.1 Initial General Excise Tax (GET) surcharge 2.2 GET surchange extensions and \"Hotel Tax\" surcharge 2.3 Federal Transit </cover>Administration's request for recovery plan 3 Route 3.1 Design 3.1.1 Farrington and Kamehameha segments 3.1.2 Airport segment 3.1.3 City Center segment 3.2 Stations 3.2.1 List of stations 3.3 Rail Operations Center 4 Rolling stock 4."},"time":73},"model_calls":61,"document_judgments":36,"relevance_3":13,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
